 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Back in the kitchen, Chef Barinov demands a dedicated restroom for his cooks, but Mikhail counters by listing every missing menu, meat shortage, and cockroach he knows about. Listen to their exchange.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Слушай, давай скажи мне сейчас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Простите, что же я игнорирую?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Я два месяца прошу туалет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Туалет надо сначала заслужить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Мы работаем лучше всех здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Да? А ну, пошли.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Мидии сегодня привезли? Нет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Где меню для завтрака?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Почему здесь недостача по мясу?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Санитарные книжки не у всех.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Ты просто за мной следишь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Я знаю всё в моём отеле.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "На твоей кухне есть тараканы.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Слушай, давай скажи мне сейчас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Listen, tell me right now.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'listen' and finishing on 'now'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Простите, что же я игнорирую?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Excuse me, what exactly am I ignoring?' Mikhail raises the pitch on 'I ignore' to turn the phrase into a direct spoken question. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Я два месяца прошу туалет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I have been asking for a restroom for two months.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'I' before landing on 'restroom'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Туалет надо сначала заслужить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A restroom must be earned first.' Mikhail brings out the contrast between 'restroom' and 'need' in a few short words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Мы работаем лучше всех здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We work better than everyone here.' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'we', while 'here' completes the thought. Mikhail answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Да? А ну, пошли.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yeah? Come on then, let's go.' Mikhail anchors the line on 'yes', while 'to go' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Мидии сегодня привезли? Нет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did they bring the mussels today? No.' The grammar packs 'mussels' and 'no' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Где меню для завтрака?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Where is the menu for breakfast?' Notice how Russian expresses 'where' and 'breakfast' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Почему здесь недостача по мясу?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why is there a meat shortage here?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'why' before landing on 'meat'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Санитарные книжки не у всех.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Not everyone has their health booklets.' Notice how Russian expresses 'health' and 'everyone' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Ты просто за мной следишь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You are simply spying on me.' Chef Barinov addresses the listener with the informal singular 'you' alongside 'you spy'. Mikhail answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Я знаю всё в моём отеле.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I know everything in my hotel.' Mikhail brings out the contrast between 'I' and 'know' in a few short words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "На твоей кухне есть тараканы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
